{
  "en": "# Why `Sudo`?\n\n- **Version:** `{version}`\n- **Developer:** [@tutosrive](https://github.com/tutosrive)\n- **Project:** Why `Sudo`?\n- **Copyright:** © 2026 - tutosrive. All Rights Reserved.\n\n**What is Why `Sudo`?**\n\n*Why `Sudo`?* is a software project designed to provide users with immediate access to a comprehensive reference of approximately 1,840 Linux commands. It offers detailed information including command meanings, syntax, and usage context, enabling efficient interaction with Linux-based systems through a centralized and structured knowledge base.\n\n### **PROPRIETARY AND CONFIDENTIAL NOTICE**\n\nThis software, including all source code, documentation, and digital assets associated with **\"Why `Sudo`?\"**, is the sole and exclusive property of **tutosrive**.\n\nAny unauthorized access, use, reproduction, or distribution of this software is strictly prohibited without express written consent from the copyright holder.\n\n### By installing or using this application, you agree to the following terms:\n\n- **Restricted License:** You are granted a personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable license to use this software for its intended purposes as provided via official distribution channels.\n- **Prohibited Actions:** You may not modify, copy, distribute, sell, sublicense, or create derivative works based on this software.\n- **No Reverse Engineering:** Decompilation, disassembly, or reverse engineering of the application’s binary code or logic is strictly forbidden.\n- **Intellectual Property:** All trademarks, logos, and brand names, including **\"Why `Sudo`?\"** and **\"tutosrive\"**, are protected under intellectual property laws."
